          "Recount texts chronicle personal experiences and past events in the order they occurred. The social function of a recount is to inform or entertain the audience with a true story. A standard recount begins with an orientation that provides background information about who, where, and when.",
          "The events section of a recount details the occurrences chronologically using past tense verbs. Writers use conjunctions of time such as after that, suddenly, and meanwhile to link sentences smoothly. Vivid action verbs make the narrative engaging for the reader.",
          "Regular past tense verbs form their past forms by adding ed to the base verb. Irregular verbs undergo internal vowel changes or remain completely unchanged in the past tense. Mastery of both verb types is essential for accurate written and spoken storytelling.",
          "A personal comment or reorientation concludes the recount text by summarizing the author's feelings. Expressions such as it was a trip of a lifetime or I will never forget that moment provide closure. This final section reflects on the significance of the experienced journey.",
          "Sensory details regarding sights, sounds, and emotions enrich personal recounts and create imagery. Describing the roaring waves, the delicious spicy aroma of local food, or the feeling of exhaustion enhances realism. These descriptive elements transform a basic report into a compelling narrative."
