        "title": "Giving Instructions and Recipe Steps",
        "paragraphs": [
          "Procedural texts provide step-by-step instructions on how to make or do something. The text structure typically consists of a goal statement, a list of required ingredients or materials, and a sequence of steps. Clear procedures ensure the reader successfully achieves the desired outcome.",
          "Imperative sentences form the core of procedural instructions by starting directly with base verbs. Commands such as chop the onions, boil the water, and stir the mixture dictate immediate action. Omitting subject pronouns creates a direct and authoritative instructional tone.",
