        "title": "Expressing Intentions and Future Plans",
        "paragraphs": [
          "Expressing future intentions requires specific grammatical structures beyond the simple present tense. The phrase be going to is utilized for premeditated plans and decisions made prior to speaking. Speakers use this form when they have already organized their upcoming actions.",
          "The modal verb will expresses spontaneous decisions, promises, and predictions about the future. When a speaker makes a choice at the exact moment of speech, will is the appropriate choice. Distinguishing between will and be going to is essential for accurate future time expression.",
