          "Modal verbs of necessity such as must, have to, and should dictate mandatory compliance in announcements. For instance, all visitors must report to the security desk establishes a strict rule. Ignoring these modal obligations often results in penalties or denied entry.",
          "Conditional warning structures often use if clauses to outline the consequences of dangerous behavior. Sentences like if the alarm sounds, evacuate the building immediately link actions to safety protocols. This structure ensures people understand the cause-and-effect relationship of emergencies.",
